# The curated restricted catalog: what deny-unless-allowed admits on its own. Every entry is
# TLS-inspected, GET and HEAD only, plus the POSTs its named allowances permit; SECURITY.md,
# "Reading without being able to write", has what each allowance opens and what the inspection
# costs and buys.
#
# Before adding a host, answer all five: why does an arbitrary project need it by default; what
# sandbox data could be sent to it; does it expose an unauthenticated write endpoint; which
# treatment — and which tags — do its operations call for; and could it be project-specific
# (.ko-agent-sandbox/egress/) instead? This list stays a small set of intentional data
# recipients; it never grows by accumulation.
# git repositories: git clone / pull use fetch, which is POST .../git-upload-pack
+host github.com   allow=git-fetch
+host codeberg.org allow=git-fetch
+host gitlab.com   allow=git-fetch

